# PHY-012 — source identifiability of A7 and composition

**Scientific status: PASS_NONIDENTIFIABILITY_THEOREM_AND_NEW_SOURCE_OBLIGATION.**

## Exact operator nonuniqueness

For a real symmetric D12-invariant circulant operator on 12 labels, Fourier sectors `k=1,...,5` are two-dimensional and `k=6` is one-dimensional. Imposing:

- positive semidefiniteness;
- removal of the uniform `k=0` mode;
- rank seven;

still does not select the FIN operator.

Rank seven requires `k=6` plus **any three** of the five two-dimensional sectors. Hence there are

`C(5,3)=10`

distinct support families before any positive eigenweights are chosen.

Even after externally fixing the FIN support `{3,4,5,6}`, positive weights satisfy

`lambda3,lambda4,lambda5,lambda6 > 0`.

Fixing the trace adds only

`2 lambda3 + 2 lambda4 + 2 lambda5 + lambda6 = T`,

leaving a **three-dimensional positive family**. Without trace normalization there are four positive weights, while the static transformation `A -> cA, g -> g/c` supplies one scale gauge, again leaving three shape ratios.

Explicit same-trace operators on the same support and on a different admissible support were constructed and checked to remain PSD, centered, rank seven and D12 invariant while differing substantially from A7.

## Composition is independently unsourced

PHY-003 already provides a nonlinear witness: retained-mean coupling and full-p coupling share the same isolated FIN core and zero-coupling limit, yet their pair distributions differ by TV **0.0454045**.

The cell graph is also not selected by single-cell D12 symmetry. Within retained-mean coupling only products `c_xy=kappa*w_xy` enter, so `kappa` versus edge-weight normalization contains a global gauge.

## New typed source obligation

`SO-PHY-012-01`:

Provide a **target-blind** rule that maps declared pre-composition FIN data (or one explicitly new fine relational observable) to:

1. cell-cell support;
2. edge-strength ratios;
3. interaction functional class;

while being equivariant under cell relabeling and internal D12/common-feature-frame gauge.

The rule and its free parameters must be frozen before revealing desired A7 spectral ratios or downstream locality/geometry scores. It must transfer across at least two carrier sizes/topologies and predict a held-out spectral or response relation without retuning.

## Decision

D12 symmetry + positivity + centering + rank do **not** derive A7. The isolated FIN core does **not** derive a unique composition. The source lane remains open only through the new typed, target-independent obligation above.
